the$  Game Help forum at Caesar III Heaven  Game versionH  This file was created using the U.S. edition of Caesar III version 1.1    General informationl  The worksheet name will be the level (1-11) followed by "p" for a peaceful assignment or "m" for a military &  assignment, followed by the city name.  o  Starting conditionsB  Level and Rank. Ranges from Level 1 (Citizen) to Level 11 (Caesar)^  Climate, type of wild animals (wolves, sheep or zebra). If Rome supplies wheat, this is noted.  Start date (month and year))  Starting funds for each difficulty level.'  Prices (at the start of the assignment)m  Lists import and export prices for all goods in the game (whether the goods appear in the assignment or not).;  City status. Lists our city and all cities that will trade.^  "Cost" is the cost to open the trade route.  "L/W" indicates if this is a Land or Water route.j  "Trade quota" show the maximum amount of each type of goods that the city sells (positive numbers) or buys)  (negative numbers) in each calendar year.  Local ResourcesB  Lists the food and raw materials that can be produced by the city.D  Lists the workshops that are allowed at the start of the assignment.M  Lists all the other types of buildings that are available in this assignment.+  Goals: lists each goal for this assignment.  Terrain mapsJ  The legend at the top left of each map shows examples of all map features.  TerrainL  "Shore" is the shallow water where only docks, ship yards, etc can be built.8  A few non-terrain features such as roads are also shown.n  If the assignment starts with buildings already on the map, the buildings are shown as boxes labeled with the T  type of building.  For 1x1 buildings, the first letter of the building type is used.%  Road and river entry and exit points.  Herd and fishing points.  Caesar III Career Path  Level  "Peaceful" assignments  "Military" assignments  The New Governor  Citizen  A Village is Born  First training assignment  Clerk  